smY","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-06T08:02:52Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T08:02:52Z","body":"I'd also like to try adding table borders and even/odd row backgrounds, as in the online documentation. But I've left that for a future PR, as the current state seems like a self-contained improvement, and table changes could introduce bugs and are controversial (as they make property/method lists less compact due to padding).\r\n\r\n> I would still try to make the primary HRs more subtle (give them the same color as secondary HRs, but keep their thicker width).\r\n\r\nI chose the accent color because the online documentation also uses a bright color instead of gray. I'll try to make them less bright by reducing the opacity. As it is now:\r\n\r\n```c++\r\ntheme_cache.primary_hr_color = Color(theme_cache.title_color, 0.5);\r\ntheme_cache.secondary_hr_color = Color(theme_cache.comment_color, 0.25);\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3858680216/reactions","t